write(14,'en',{}, {1:'The Hebrew describes lying down with his fathers and active plural buriers; BSB says rested and expresses burial passively.',4:'The Hebrew has singular commandment; BSB uses plural commandments.',5:'The Hebrew says the kingdom rested before him; BSB says under him.',6:'The Hebrew leaves the builder unnamed and calls the period years; BSB names Asa and says days.',7:'The Hebrew says the land is still before us; BSB says still ours.',9:'The Hebrew says a thousand thousands and has singular he came; BSB uses 1,000,000 and plural they advanced.',10:'The Hebrew has a plural subject for drawing up for battle; BSB continues with Asa as the singular subject.',11:'The Hebrew speaks of helping between the great and one without strength; BSB explicitly says helping the powerless against the mighty.',13:'The Hebrew names the people with Asa and leaves the plunderers implicit; BSB calls the pursuers his army and explicitly names the people of Judah as plunderers. The force with the LORD is called His camp rather than His army.',15:'The Hebrew says tents of livestock and uses a capturing verb; BSB says tents of the herdsmen and carried off.'})
